  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The RMS&nbsp;speed of a gas at a given temperature is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>rms</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>.</p><p>Therefore, to double the RMS speed, the temperature should be increased to four times the initial temperature. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>28</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>The volume of the vessel will remain&nbsp;the same therefore, the process is an isochoric process. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>900</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9360</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
